        "sample": "I would like to talk about a meal I will never forget, which I had about two years ago at my grandmother's house in the countryside. It was a family celebration for my grandfather's seventieth birthday, so about twenty relatives were there, including cousins I had not seen for years.\n\nMy grandmother had spent the whole morning cooking. The table was covered with dishes: a slow-cooked lamb curry, rice with saffron, fresh salads, homemade bread and a wonderful chickpea dish with spinach. Everything was made from ingredients grown in her own garden, so the flavours were incredibly fresh. For dessert we had rice pudding with cinnamon, which has always been my favourite.\n\nI enjoyed the meal for two main reasons. First, the food itself was outstanding; every dish tasted of care and experience, and nothing came from a packet. Second, and more importantly, the atmosphere was wonderful. We sat outside under a large tree, talking and laughing for hours, and nobody looked at a phone. My grandfather told stories about his childhood, and the meal became a way of bringing three generations together. Whenever I taste that curry now, I remember that afternoon, which is why the meal means so much more to me than just good food. It is a tradition I hope our family never loses, however busy modern life becomes."
